      ":question/problem": "![](images/01/01b742fa8f4bf42597e8653cf6b379537d95c3789743a564064a768ca343d197.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What is the value of $a+k?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.$ This means that $k=1$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}+1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,2.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}+1 \\\\ 2.5 & =\\frac{a}{1}+1 \\\\ 1.5 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=1+1.5=2.5.$"
    },
    {
