      ":question/problem": "![](images/4f/4f8e1c3db4120b0fcd8491a850d238b81452fb0294145a2062f96c4655164a04.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x}+k.$ What is the value of $a+k?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1.5.$ This means that $k=-1.5$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x}-1.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,-2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x}-1.5 \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{a}{1}-1.5 \\\\ -0.5 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+k=-0.5-1.5=-2.$"
